data medium_structure_grammar_classifier_note: String = "no-smuggled-programs wall (HALF B): this lens is a GRAMMAR CLASSIFIER over substrate string literals, REPLACING the marker heuristic (medium_syntax_markers + emit-fn/string-op walks DELETED in one motion, both the .dag markers and the Rust text.contains in medium_structure_census.rs). The seed (medium_structure_literal_parts_facts, ruling R1b grammar/language-ignorant) enumerates RawLine.text / Heredoc.body field-expression PARTS as neutral [Const|Hole]; this lens applies the TYPE-STRUCTURAL language gate and runs bash_composition_recognizer. A composition of a modeled language = typed/located/COUNTED Violation; an atom = Clean; the undecidable residue = counted AmbiguousParse (DecodeFidelity). ConstructionJustification = WallAfterGrounding (marker heuristic -> grammar classifier); the genuine-Unknown AmbiguousParse residue is RatchetForever."

data medium_structure_type_structural_gate_note: String = "The language-decision gate is the ShellStmt coproduct (dag/extdeps/languages/bash/program.dag): every variant is MODELED structure EXCEPT the two String-carrying smuggling vectors RawLine.text and Heredoc.body. RawLine.text is definitionally bash. Heredoc.body language depends on the target, but the emit (program.dag) hardwires cat to path (the body is WRITTEN TO A FILE as data, never piped to an interpreter), so the type cannot name a language, giving AmbiguousParse cause NoLanguageDecision interim (UNRESOLVED-language framing: a heredoc writing a bash script then exec IS smuggled but the model cannot see the deferred exec; a target-resolution follow-up can reclassify bash-target heredoc to Violation, so counted Ambiguous rows stay a LIVE ledger, not a permanent silent gap)."

data medium_structure_path_a_supersession_note: String = "PATH A SUPERSEDED (decision history, parent+operator reconciled 2026-07-14): Path A (tighten the extdeps/languages path-exemption to grammar-rows-only + roster the retry_eagain EAGAIN blob + baseline 62->63) was OPERATOR-SIGNED 2026-07-14, then SUPERSEDED by the type-structural-gate finding, VERIFIED-BY both sessions independently in-tree (executor stern-eagle-53 and manager sharp-crane-105): retry_eagain_seg_a..h4 (src/v2/extdeps/languages/bash.dag) are String fns fed to span(text: ...) rows in retry_eagain_bash_lex() = grammar-row LEX SPELLINGS (the AUTHORITY the wall points AT, decomposed by emit slice-0), NEVER a RawLine.text/Heredoc.body site, so the type-structural gate NEVER classifies them. Therefore Path A rosters/baseline-bumps NOTHING real; the gate SUPERSEDES the coarse path-exemption. Consequences applied honestly (NOT a silent removal): (1) no EAGAIN roster entry, no 62->63 bump; (2) the whole coarse path-exemption is DELETED — it exempted zero classified sites under the gate (no RawLine/Heredoc CONSTRUCTION exists in any formerly-exempt dir: extdeps/github, extdeps/languages, compiler/05_emit, compiler/06_translate, self_host/candidate_generation, communication/medium), and a dead exemption is the inert-lens-is-a-lie failure; removing it also closes a would-be silent gap (a future RawLine in an exempt dir is now caught). Operator was notified of the supersession in parallel; a one-line revert restores Path A if objected."

data medium_bash_sink_targets: List<String> = ["RawLine.text", "Heredoc.body"]

type RawLiteralPart {
  is_hole: Bool
  text: String
}

type RawLiteralPartsFact {
  path: String
  constructor: String
  field: String
  parts: List<RawLiteralPart>
}

data empty_skeleton_parts: List<SkeletonPart> = []

fn part_to_skeleton(p: RawLiteralPart) -> SkeletonPart {
  if p.is_hole {
    HolePart
  } else {
    ConstPart { text: p.text }
  }
}

fn parts_to_skeleton(parts: List<RawLiteralPart>) -> LiteralSkeleton {
  LiteralSkeleton {
    parts: fold_list(
      xs: parts,
      empty: empty_skeleton_parts,
      cons: fn(acc, p) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: part_to_skeleton(p: p)) }
    )
  }
}

fn constructor_field_matches(fact: RawLiteralPartsFact, ctor: String, field: String) -> Bool {
  (fact.constructor == ctor) && (fact.field == field)
}

fn classify_raw_literal_fact(fact: RawLiteralPartsFact) -> BashCompositionDisposition {
  if constructor_field_matches(fact: fact, ctor: "RawLine", field: "text") {
    classify_bash_skeleton(sk: parts_to_skeleton(parts: fact.parts))
  } else {
    AmbiguousParse { cause: NoLanguageDecision }
  }
}

data medium_scope_test_construction_exclusion_note: String = "SCOPE (explicit, documented — NOT a silent narrowing; matches the ci_layer_roots.dag documented-exclusion idiom): the live scan roots are the PRODUCTION SUBSTRATE (std/extdeps/compiler/tools/gunbc/workflow/lens). test/claim is DELIBERATELY OUT OF SCOPE because the wall's subject is substrate SMUGGLING, and a test that CONSTRUCTS a RawLine to exercise the bash fold is building the escape hatch to TEST it, not smuggling a program. COUNTED/visible (the excluded would-be-violation set): src/v2/test/claim/bash_command_fold_test.dag constructs a RawLine.text of do_verify-newline-more (a 2-line composition that WOULD classify Violation) plus several single-command RawLines (Clean) and Heredoc bodies (AmbiguousParse); flagging a TEST of the escape hatch is a category error. Fixtures (planted/perturb, src/v2/test/fixture/medium_structure_scan) are passed as EXPLICIT perturb roots, so this default scope does not affect them. Confirmed: no PRODUCTION emit path constructs RawLine from a LITERAL in an excluded dir — the machinery sites (bash program emit) construct from dynamic tokens, not literals. Dissolve-on: test-construction of escape-hatch values gets a typed marker so it is distinguishable in-scope, or the vocab.NarrowingReason enum gains a TestFixtureConstruction variant this note is promoted to."

